# Why the "study-endpoint and report vocabulary" section exists
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-09-04. These reached the store as clinical entities and were typed
# irreconcilably across abstracts -- "outcomes" as InformationEntity, Occurrent,
# ProcessBoundary and Quality; "adverse events" as four categories at once. They
# are not clinical entities typed badly, they are the vocabulary a paper uses to
# describe its own design and results, and the ontology has no place for them.
# Surfaced by BaseHierarchy.irreconcilable; see INSTRUCTIONS rule 9.
#
# Moved out of the literal on 2026-09-25: the literal became a generated view of
# the gate (rule 40) and only the one-line section headers survive a round trip.
